{
  "id": 447167823,
  "iid": 23248,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "DHCP: Handle more than one user class in MS Option 77",
  "description": "RFC 2131 Section 4.1 states that \"Options may appear only once,\nunless otherwise specified in the options document,\" and that\nmultiple instances of the same option are concatenated. RFC 3396\ndescribed that concatenation in more detail.\n\n[MS-DHCPE] describes a variant Option 77 (User Class Option) that\ndoes not match RFC 3004. Section 2.2.6.2 ddoes mention that \"one\nor more User Class Options\" are contained in the DHCP ACK message.\nPer RFC 3396, these are concatenated, so the handling of the MS\nversion need to handle multiple User Class Options as the RFC version\ndoes.\n\nAlso, fix an encoding error in the User Class Binary Data. ENC_STRING\nis not an encoding (though if it alone appears, effectively ENC_ASCII\nis used, which is why the error is not always noticed.) However, per\nthe name this is binary data that may be, but not necessarily,\nprintable. Thus, make it a FT_BYTES field but show it if printable.\n\nThe file in !11628 has more than one user class option and needs this.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
